   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## inpaint.json\n\nInpaint\n\nInpaint (core InpaintModelConditioning). IMPORTANT: the raw output drifts ~5/255 outside the mask (VAE round-trip) -> always ImageCompositeMasked with the mask back onto the original for pixel-exact preservation outside.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S5** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E8** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*\n\n**Mask softener (added 2026-11-16):** the mask passes a `GrowMaskWithBlur` before conditioning - shipped at **expand 0 / blur 0 = the E8-measured hard-mask behavior**, identical output (verified by re-run, same seed). Raise the knobs for object edits: **grow first** (8-32 px - covers paint-line imprecision, prevents ghost remnants of the old content at full strength), **then blur** (2-8 px - blends the seam). Blur alone puts half-strength exactly on your painted line - that is where ghosts come from. Painted masks are binary (MaskEditor); softness is deliberately a graph knob, not a drawing skill. The composite below still blends with the original un-feathered mask, so the untouched region keeps the E8 guarantee."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## inpaint.json\n\nInpaint\n\nInpaint (core InpaintModelConditioning). IMPORTANT: the raw output drifts ~5/255 outside the mask (VAE round-trip) -> always ImageCompositeMasked with the mask back onto the original for pixel-exact preservation outside.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S5** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E8** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*\n\n**Mask softener (added 2026-11-16):** the mask passes a `GrowMaskWithBlur` before conditioning - shipped at **expand 0 / blur 0 = the E8-measured hard-mask behavior**, identical output (verified by re-run, same seed). Raise the knobs for object edits: **grow first** (8-32 px - covers paint-line imprecision, prevents ghost remnants of the old content at full strength), **then blur** (2-8 px - blends the seam). Blur alone puts half-strength exactly on your painted line - that is where ghosts come from. Painted masks are binary (MaskEditor); softness is deliberately a graph knob, not a drawing skill. The composite below still blends with the original un-feathered mask, so the untouched region keeps the E8 guarantee."
   },
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  },
